```
main.tsx
  └── App.tsx
        ├── QueryClientProvider     # TanStack Query (retry: 1, no refetch on focus)
        └── ThemeProvider           # MUI theme from @/theme
              └── CssBaseline
              └── { children }      # Currently: placeholder Container
```

When implementing phases, wrap in this order (outer → inner):

`QueryClientProvider` → `ThemeModeProvider` → `ThemeProvider` → `CssBaseline` → `RouterProvider` → layout

## Environment Variables

| Variable | Purpose | Example |
|----------|---------|---------|
| `VITE_API_URL` | Backend base URL (browser calls) | `http://localhost:8090` |
| `VITE_APP_NAME` | Display name in UI | `Binder App` |
| `VITE_DEV_PORT` | Vite dev server port | `3000` |

- Copy `.env.example` → `.env.development` for local/Docker dev.
- Docker prod build passes `VITE_API_URL` and `VITE_APP_NAME` as build args (baked into bundle).
- Backend CORS expects `FRONTEND_HOST=http://localhost:3000` in dev.

## Backend Integration

Sibling project: `../binder_app_backend/`

| Concern | Detail |
|---------|--------|
| Auth | JWT in `httpOnly` cookie `access_token` |
| Fetch | Always `credentials: 'include'` on authenticated requests |
| Session | `GET /user/me` returns profile + active companies |
| Roles | `Superadmin`, `Editor`, `Viewer` (backend `Role` enum) |
| Swagger | `http://localhost:8090/api` (dev) |

### Known backend routes (do not invent endpoints)

**Auth** (`/auth`):

- `POST /auth/login`, `POST /auth/logout`
- `POST /auth/password/forgot`, `POST /auth/password/reset`

**User** (`/user`):

- `GET /user/me` — authenticated profile
- Additional user CRUD routes exist on backend — check `binder_app_backend/src/user/` before implementing UI

**Other modules** on backend: `company/`, `invite/` — implement frontend pages only when backend endpoints are confirmed in source.

